#: ../../../../examples/tutorials/basics/text.py:65
msgid ""
"<div class=\"sphx-glr-thumbcontainer\" tooltip=\"The frame parameter of the "
"plotting methods of the pygmt.Figure class can control which axes should be "
"plotted and optionally show annotations, tick marks, and gridlines. By "
"default, all 4 axes are plotted, along with annotations and tick marks "
"(denoted W, S, E, N). Lowercase versions (w, s, e, n) can be used to denote "
"to only plot the axes with tick marks. We can also only plot the axes "
"without annotations and tick marks using l (left axis), r (right axis), t "
"(top axis), b (bottom axis). When frame is used to change the frame "
"settings, any axes that are not defined using one of these three options are "
"not drawn.\">"
msgstr ""

